# Plain documentation

Read `.cursor/skills/ecm-ai-language/SKILL.md` when writing documentation, diagram labels, or interface copy. Code identifiers use readable-names.

- Name the actor and action. Use ordinary verbs: use, check, save, compare, send.
- Avoid leverage, unlock, robust, seamless, holistic.
- Explain purpose before implementation details. Prefer a clear sentence to a compressed noun stack.
- Keep one term for one meaning. Show the current identifier beside the explanation when the reader needs to find it.
